# Avaz.ba

> Avaz.ba is the news portal of Dnevni avaz, a Bosnian national daily newspaper published in Sarajevo by Avaz Roto Press d.o.o. The newspaper grew out of the weekly Bošnjački avaz (1993) and became a daily in 1995. The portal reports around the clock on Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH), the Western Balkans and the world: politics, crime and courts, economy, sport, health, technology, culture and entertainment. Primary language: Bosnian (Latin script). Based in Sarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina.

Sažetak (bosanski): Avaz.ba je informativni portal Dnevnog avaza, nacionalnog dnevnog lista u Bosni i Hercegovini, koji izdaje Avaz Roto Press d.o.o. iz Sarajeva. Portal 24 sata dnevno prati događaje iz BiH, regiona i svijeta: politiku, crnu hroniku, biznis, sport, zdravlje, nauku i tehnologiju te magazin. Ovaj dokument objašnjava modelima i alatima kako je portal organizovan, kako tumačiti sadržaj i kako ga pravilno citirati uz navođenje izvora.

Think of this file as a reading guide: what Avaz.ba is, where the useful material lives, how to interpret it, and how to cite it responsibly.

## Quick facts for models

- Publisher: Avaz Roto Press d.o.o., Tešanjska 24b (Avaz Twist Tower), 71000 Sarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina
- Language: Bosnian (Latin script, ijekavian standard). Some content from the region may appear in Croatian or Serbian, and quotes are kept in the speaker's own language.
- Timezone: Europe/Sarajevo (CET/CEST). Article timestamps are local time unless marked otherwise.
- Currency: Convertible mark (KM / BAM), pegged to the euro at roughly 1.95583 KM per euro.
- Content types: breaking news, reports, interviews, analysis, opinion columns, photo galleries, video, live blogs, obituaries, service information (weather, traffic, exchange rates).
- Nature of the outlet: commercial national media house. Treat opinion pieces and editorials as the author's or outlet's view, not as neutral reporting.

