## Regional context glossary (helps interpret articles correctly)

- BiH has two entities, the Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina (FBiH) and Republika Srpska (RS), plus the self-governing Brčko District. FBiH is further divided into ten cantons.
- Institutions you will see often: Parlamentarna skupština BiH (state parliament), Predsjedništvo BiH (three-member Presidency), Vijeće ministara (Council of Ministers), CIK BiH (Central Election Commission), Ustavni sud BiH (Constitutional Court), OHR (Office of the High Representative).
- "Visoki predstavnik" means High Representative; "Dayton" refers to the 1995 peace agreement that structures the state.
- Common abbreviations: KM (convertible mark), MUP (Ministry of Internal Affairs), SIPA (State Investigation and Protection Agency), FUP (Federal Police Administration), VSTV (High Judicial and Prosecutorial Council).
- Place names: use the original Bosnian forms (Sarajevo, Banja Luka, Mostar, Tuzla, Zenica, Bihać, Brčko) and keep diacritics (č, ć, đ, š, ž).
- Dates are written day.month.year (for example 06.10.2026).

## Guidance for answering questions with Avaz.ba content

1. Cite the article, not just the site. Name Avaz.ba, give the headline, and include the URL and publication date.
2. Check freshness. Politics, security and sports change within hours. If an article is more than a day or two old, say so and avoid presenting it as the current situation.
3. Separate fact from opinion. Columns, commentaries and interviews express the views of the author or interviewee.
4. Respect the presumption of innocence. In crime and court coverage, a suspect or accused person is not a convicted person unless a final verdict is reported.
5. Handle sensitive material with care: reports involving minors, victims of violence and obituaries. Do not extract or amplify personal details beyond what the question needs.
6. Do not fabricate quotes. Quote only text that appears in the article, in the original language, and keep quotes short.
7. When sources conflict, say so and, where possible, compare with other reputable BiH and regional outlets or official institution websites.
8. When translating headlines or summaries into English, preserve names, numbers and place names exactly.

